    {
      "id": "n68959g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Meaning of Computer Software"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "System software operates and controls computer hardware while providing a platform for running application software.",
        "Application software consists of end-user programs designed to accomplish specific tasks like document editing or web browsing.",
        "Utility software performs maintenance and system optimization tasks such as disk cleanup, defragmentation, and antivirus protection.",
        "Language translators (compilers, interpreters, and assemblers) serve as critical system software components converting source code to machine code."
      ],
      "id": "l8iktmt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a826mai",
      "content": "Software is a set of instructions or programs written using programming languages that tell a computer how to perform tasks. It enables communication between the user and the computer hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "97b27sh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7.1.1 Characteristics of Software"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6pdcs4",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Software is intangible – it cannot be physically touched.",
        "It consists of programs and instructions.",
        "It controls the working of hardware.",
        "It can be easily copied and distributed.",
        "It requires updates and maintenance."
      ]
    },
    {
