    {
      "id": "4i41y5g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.5 Utility Software"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufue1yd",
      "content": "Utility software is a type of system software that helps maintain, manage, and optimize the performance of a computer system."
    },
    {
      "id": "6c2ly33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7.5.1 Functions of Utility Software"
    },
    {
      "id": "98nn70v",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Improves system performance.",
        "Protects the system from viruses.",
        "Manages files and storage.",
        "Backs up important data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions often ask to categorize software: Compilers, Device Drivers, and Operating Systems are System Software, while Antivirus and Disk Defragmenters are Utility Software.",
        "Compilers convert high-level code to machine code in one go, whereas Interpreters translate line-by-line.",
        "Application software cannot run independently without the underlying System Software."
      ],
      "id": "3rp9t18"
    },
